pGate\": {\n      \"policy\": \"resolveAgentBrowserSessionEffectPolicy\",\n      \"callSite\": \"agent-browser-tool.ts (assertSessionEffectAllowed)\",\n      \"actions\": [\n        \"click\",\n        \"type\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": \"Main-owned managed session under external/unknown provenance\"\n    },\n    \"actions\": [\n      \"status\",\n      \"navigate\",\n      \"waitForSelector\",\n      \"click\",\n      \"type\",\n      \"evaluate\",\n      \"screenshot\",\n      \"command\",\n      \"close\",\n      \"getConsoleMessages\"\n    ],\n    \"residualNoSessionGate\": [\n      \"evaluate\",\n      \"command\",\n      \"close\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"gates\": {\n    \"existingBrowserProvenance\": {\n      \"command\": \"openclaw_runtime: run-vitest agent-browser-external-access-policy.test.ts agent-browser-tool.provenance.test.ts agent-browser-provenance-wiring.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"files\": 3,\n      \"tests\": 42,\n      \"failed\": 0\n    },\n    \"ledgerGuard\": {\n      \"command\": \"vitest run tests/unit/browser-effect-boundary-ledger.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"files\": 1,\n      \"tests\": 5,\n      \"failed\": 0\n    },\n    \"typecheckTest\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm run typecheck:test\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    \"lintTouched\": {\n      \"command\": \"eslint tests/unit/browser-effect-boundary-ledger.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    \"harnessValidate\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm harness validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-browser-effect-boundary.md\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"result\": \"Spec is valid\"\n    },\n    \"harnessDryRun\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm harness run --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-browser-effect-boundary.md --dry-run\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"result\": \"pass\"\n    },\n    \"commsReplay\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm run comms:replay\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    \"commsCompare\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm run comms:compare\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"result\": \"all PASS, 0.00% delta\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"residual\": {\n    \"evaluateCommandClose\": \"Side-effecting actions evaluate / command / close are not covered by the click/type session-ownership gate; they only pass the connection-mode gate. Recorded as residual, not claimed covered.\",\n    \"scope\": \"agent_browser tool egress only; renderer/other browser entry points are out of scope.\",\n    \"noNetworkRuleChange\": \"SSRF / private-network / kill switch rules are independent and unchanged.\"\n  },\n  \"independentVerification\": {\n    \"executed\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"policy unit + source wiring pin\",\n    \"detail\": \"The guard resolves both policies across provenance x connection-mode matrices and pins the tool wiring (external-access before invoke; session gate only on click/type). No separate second-agent verifier role was run.\",\n    \"separateVerifierAgent\": false\n  },\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"source-gate\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"external/derived-untrusted/missing/invalid provenance is denied auto-connect/cdp/external-profile; managed allowed; trusted system/operator unrestricted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"session-ownership\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"click/type under external/unknown provenance require a Main-owned managed session; otherwise denied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"per-action-ledger\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"Every action recorded; only click/type carry the extra session-ownership gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"residual-recorded\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"evaluate/command/close recorded as residual (side-effecting but not session-gated); no over-claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-weakening\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"SSRF/private-network/kill switch untouched; no third policy introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"clean-candidate-gates\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"42 existing + 5 new tests pass, typecheck:test 0, scoped lint 0, harness validate/dry-run pass, comms 0, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS verifiable.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"productLocks\": {\n    \"live_ready\": false,\n    \"product_approved\": false,\n    \"default_on\": false,\n    \"changed\": false\n  },\n  \"credentialScan\": {\n    \"files\": 2,\n    \"hits\": 0\n  },\n  \"notMeasured\": [\n    \"Live browser / real account sessions.\",\n    \"Renderer-side browser entry points.\",\n    \"A separate second-agent independent verifier role.\"\n  ],\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"pushed\": false,\n    \"pr\": null,\n    \"note\": \"Pushed with the evidence commit in the same session; see the branch's PR.\"\n  }\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s04-browser-effect-boundary.md -Raw; \"`n=== SUMS ===\"; Get-Content docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S04-SHA256SUMS -Raw'","aggregated_output":"# S04：浏览器来源、会话归属与副作用边界（台账）\n\n日期：2026-10-13（Asia/Shanghai）。包码：S04（TF-0279）。真实 provider / 真实浏览器账号调用：无。\n\n## 链路（source → policy → effect）\n\n`openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/agent-browser-tool.ts` 对**每个** action 先跑：\n- `resolveAgentBrowserExternalAccessPolicy`（来源 + connectionMode）：external/derived-untrusted/missing/invalid 来源**不得**选择 `auto-connect` / `cdp` / `external-profile`；只有 `managed` 放行。\n- `resolveAgentBrowserSessionEffectPolicy`（来源 + 会话语义）：**仅 click / type** 额外要求“会话被判定为 Main-owned managed”；否则拒绝。\n\n两条策略都在 `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/agent-browser-external-access-policy.ts`。\n\n## 每个 action 的覆盖\n\n| action | 外部来源闸门（连接模式） | 会话归属闸门（click/type 同款） | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| status | ✅ 全 action 生效 | — | 只读 |\n| navigate | ✅ | — | 受连接模式约束 |\n| waitForSelector | ✅ | — | 只读等待 |\n| click | ✅ | ✅ 仅 managed | 副作用 |\n| type | ✅ | ✅ 仅 managed | 副作用 |\n| screenshot | ✅ | — | 只读 |\n| getConsoleMessages | ✅ | — | 只读 |\n| **evaluate** | ✅ | ❌ **未接线** | 可执行页面 JS（残余） |\n| **command** | ✅ | ❌ **未接线** | 任意浏览器命令（残余） |\n| **close** | ✅ | ❌ **未接线** | 关闭会话（残余） |\n\n## 残余 residual（显式记录，不冒充已覆盖）\n\n- `evaluate` / `command` / `close` 是副作用型 action，但**没有**走 click/type 那套“会话必须 managed”的会话归属闸门；它们只受连接模式闸门约束。若 external 来源配 managed 会话，仍可执行这些 action。\n- 本台账只覆盖 `agent_browser` 工具出口；不覆盖渲染器/其他浏览器入口。\n- 不弱化 SSRF、private-network、kill switch：这些规则独立，未被本核验改动。\n\n## 边界与不做项\n\n- 只核验既有两条策略，不新建第三套策略；不改 managed/external 的既有语义。\n- 不改产品默认值/锁/approval；非真人证据。\n\r\n\n=== SUMS ===\r\nb35b8861b4e37a7f9117c40451783debd7e57d71c5298b95be18d0471208510e  docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s04-acceptance.json\n634b0d96bcd581ff8e4df39c4210b20771497ebbfd9b057217beed69f75b5c96  docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s04-browser-effect-boundary.md\ne5643434df4ef084c760063b92896acb69fe2484cc6cc8cf5fb0756801d50a16  harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-browser-effect-boundary.md\n42d481e78e431e7c9d05e52ab6e4779dc1d882b2419c22a2f95ce13a13119b1e  tests/unit/browser-effect-boundary-ledger.test.ts\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content harness/specs/tasks/credential-use-provenance-boundary.md -Raw'","aggregated_output":"---\nlifecycleStatus: archived\nid: credential-use-provenance-boundary\ntitle: Credential-use provenance boundary for image provider overrides\nscenario: gateway-backend-communication\ntaskType: runtime-bridge\nintent: Consume the existing ContentProvenance sidecar at one bounded credential-use surface: explicit cross-provider model overrides in the agent image_generate tool, without changing configured defaults, automatic fallback, or normal model authentication.\ntouchedAreas:\n  - harness/specs/tasks/credential-use-provenance-boundary.md\n  - shared/security/content-provenance.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/agent-tools.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/openclaw-tools.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/image-generate-provenance-wiring.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/image-generate-tool.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/provider-credential-use-policy.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/provider-credential-use-policy.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/image-generate-tool.credential-use-provenance.test.ts\nrequiredProfiles:\n  - fast\n  - comms\nrequiredRules:\n  - backend-communication-boundary\n  - comms-regression\n  - docs-sync\nrequiredTests:\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/provider-credential-use-policy.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/image-generate-tool.credential-use-provenance.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/image-generate-provenance-wiring.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/message-secret-read-policy.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/message-tool.provenance.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/exec-provenance-policy.test.ts\n  - openclaw_runtime/src/agents/exec-defaults.test.ts\nacceptance:\n  - The existing ContentProvenance contract remains the only source/trust enum definition.\n  - The centralized credential-use classification records this task's policy as a `narrow` enforcement point; broader credential-use coverage is still not claimed and this task enforces only the bounded image_generate provider-override path.\n  - Calls without an explicit model override keep the configured primary provider and automatic fallback behavior unchanged.\n  - Same-provider model overrides remain usable for untrusted, derived-untrusted, missing, or invalid provenance.\n  - Providers explicitly named by the operator in agents.defaults.imageGenerationModel primary or fallbacks remain usable.\n  - When no explicit image-generation model config exists, the resolved default primary provider remains usable.\n  - Untrusted, derived-untrusted, missing, or invalid provenance cannot explicitly switch image_generate to a different provider merely because credentials for that provider are discoverable.\n  - Trusted system and direct operator provenance retain the existing explicit provider/model override behavior.\n  - The source-dependent decision runs before image provider credential resolution or provider execution and never receives or reports credential values; auth-aware availability discovery may already have performed read-only configured-state checks used to preserve the resolved default provider.\n  - image_generate list/status actions, provider discovery, availability checks, duplicate guards, remote-media SSRF policy, generated-media delivery, and configured automatic fallback remain unchanged.\n  - Existing command-exec defaults, explicit fullAccess behavior, message network-send, and message secret-read behavior remain unchanged.\n  - No blanket approval, prompt rewrite, global taint engine, regex injection classifier, config field, dependency, or provider shutdown is introduced.\nexpectedUserBehavior:\n  - Normal image generation continues to use the operator-selected default provider and configured fallbacks.\n  - External or unknown content cannot silently select a different provider credential through the image_generate model argument.\n  - A direct operator request can still choose an available provider/model explicitly.\ndocs:\n  required: false\n  note: This is a narrow runtime policy refinement using existing configuration and provenance metadata; it adds no user-visible setting and does not claim complete credential-use enforcement.\n---\n\n# Implementation contract\n\nThe image generation tool resolves its default model scope using existing,\nread-only auth-aware availability checks, then resolves an explicit `model`\nargument before provider request credential lookup and provider execution.\nThis task inserts one pure, source-dependent provider decision at that boundary.\nThe decision compares the resolved requested provider with host-owned operator\nconfiguration and the authoritative provenance parser; it never inspects prompt\ntext or credential values.\n\nFor external, derived-external, missing, or invalid provenance, an explicit\nmodel override may stay on the configured provider set but may not switch to a\ncredential-bearing provider discovered only from runtime availability. Direct\noperator and trusted system sources preserve current override behavior. Other\nmodel-backed tools, automatic provider fallback, general model authentication,\nMCP, browser credentials, and all non-image credential-use paths remain\nexplicit residual scope.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
